  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You magically mark one creature you can see within range as your quarry. Until the spell ends, you deal an extra 1d6 Force damage to the target whenever you hit it with an attack roll. You also have Advantage on any Wisdom (Perception) or Wisdom (Survival) check you make to find it.</p><p>If the target drops to 0 Hit Points before this spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action to move the mark to a new creature you can see within range.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> Your Concentration can last longer with a spell slot of level 3–4 (up to 8 hours) or 5+ (up to 24 hours).</p><p><strong>midi-qol</strong>: Uses two effects — a \"Hunter's Mark\" effect applied to the target (with the <code>marked</code> status) and a transfer effect on the caster that registers a <code>DamageBonusMacro</code>. On any attack hit, the macro checks if the hit target has the <code>marked</code> status from this spell (using <code>MidiQOL.getItemFromEffectOrigin</code> to resolve through concentration effect chains) and automatically adds 1d6 Force damage. Critical hits are handled via <code>isCritical</code> on the DamageRoll. Use \"Move Mark\" (bonus action) when the marked target drops to 0 HP to re-mark a new creature without consuming a new spell slot. The Move Mark activity macro automatically removes the existing mark from the old target (found via <code>concentrationEffect.getDependents()</code>) before applying the new one.</p>",
      "chat": "<p>You magically mark one creature you can see within range as your quarry. Until the spell ends, you deal an extra 1d6 Force damage to the target whenever you hit it with an attack roll. You also have Advantage on any Wisdom (Perception) or Wisdom (Survival) check you make to find it.</p><p>If the target drops to 0 Hit Points before this spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action to move the mark to a new creature you can see within range.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> Your Concentration can last longer with a spell slot of level 3–4 (up to 8 hours) or 5+ (up to 24 hours).</p>"
    },
